## Models

### Model Reference

**Gemini 4:** In OpenCode V2, select `google/antigravity-gemini-4-neon`, `google/antigravity-gemini-4-hydrogen`,
`google/antigravity-gemini-4-carbon`, or `google/antigravity-gemini-4-argon`. OAuth uses the backend ID
listed for the selected Antigravity account and project. If its catalog omits
the model, the plugin can use a configured Gemini API key when API-key fallback
is enabled. The OpenCode model list alone does not establish account access.
Neon, Hydrogen, and Carbon support `low`, `medium`, `high`, and `xhigh`; Argon
supports `low`, `medium`, and `high`. `antigravity-gemini-4-hydrogen-sonar` is a
separate discovery-only OAuth model.

**Antigravity quota** (default routing for Claude and Gemini):

| Model | Variants | Notes |
|-------|----------|-------|
| `antigravity-gemini-3.8-flash` | low, medium, high | **Newest.** Gemini 3.8 Flash with thinking (medium default) |
| `antigravity-gemini-4-argon` | low, medium, high | 256K context, high default; minimal maps to low |
| `antigravity-gemini-4-carbon` | low, medium, high, xhigh | Gemini 4 Carbon |
| `antigravity-gemini-4-hydrogen` | low, medium, high, xhigh | Gemini 4 Hydrogen |
| `antigravity-gemini-4-neon` | low, medium, high, xhigh | Gemini 4 Neon |
| `antigravity-gemini-3-flash` | minimal, low, medium, high | Gemini 3 Flash with thinking |
| `antigravity-gemini-3.1-flash-lite` | minimal, low, medium, high | Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite with thinking |
| `antigravity-gemini-3.5-flash-lite` | minimal, low, medium, high | Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite with thinking |
| `antigravity-claude-opus-5-5` | low, medium, high | Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, 128K output, high default) |
| `antigravity-claude-sonnet-5-5` | low, medium, high | Claude Sonnet 5.5 (1M context, 128K output, high default) |
| `antigravity-claude-sonnet-4-6` | — | Claude Sonnet 4.6 |
| `antigravity-claude-opus-4-6-thinking` | low, max | Claude Opus 4.6 with extended thinking |

> Google retired Gemini 3 Pro, Gemini 3.1 Pro, and intermediate Gemini 3 Flash models from Antigravity. The plugin no longer substitutes another model for them: a request is sent under the id you picked, so a retired id fails with the backend's own error.

> **The Gemini CLI quota is gone.** Google deprecated it in favour of Antigravity, which shares the Antigravity quota. The bare CLI models (`gemini-3.8-flash`, `gemini-3-flash-preview`, and friends) are no longer listed — the `antigravity-` variants serve the same workloads — and a request for one is still routed through Antigravity. The quota check no longer fetches or shows Gemini CLI quota, and the `cli_first` option is removed.

**Antigravity SDK / Gemini API projects** (API-key backed; used by API-key auth, or as OAuth fallback when configured):

The official Antigravity SDK uses `GEMINI_API_KEY` for local Gemini access. This plugin now supports that path directly for Gemini models while keeping OAuth accounts for Antigravity and Claude.

> **Routing Behavior:**
> - **OAuth Antigravity-first (default):** Gemini models use Antigravity quota across OAuth accounts.
> - **Antigravity SDK / Gemini API:** API-key auth, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, or configured `agy_sdk.cloud_projects` route Gemini requests through the public Gemini API.
> - When the OAuth Antigravity quota is exhausted on every account, configured `agy_sdk.cloud_projects` are used as backup capacity before failing if `agy_sdk.enabled: true`, `agy_sdk.api_key_fallback: true`, and usable API-key credentials are present.
> - Claude and image models always use Antigravity.

**Using variants:**
```bash
opencode run "Hello" --model=google/antigravity-claude-opus-4-6-thinking --variant=max
```

For details on variant configuration and thinking levels, see [docs/MODEL-VARIANTS.md](docs/MODEL-VARIANTS.md).

